dropped
  go      the middleware stack and its options (s3.Options.APIOptions' entries, Logger, ClientLogMode, AppID, Interceptors, AuthSchemeResolver, ResponseChecksumValidation, RequestChecksumCalculation: covered by `objects/checksums`), the endpoint resolver's parameters and its V1 form, the waiters' option records, the paginators' option records, manager's pools and buffers beyond `multipart/managed`: plumbing an interface or a closure would need
  go      minio-go's MinIO-only extensions beyond the S3 API: AppendObject, PutObjectFanOut, PutObjectsSnowball, PromptObject, ListenBucketNotification, ListenNotification, GetBucketQOS, SetBucketQOS, GetBucketQOSMetrics, NewQOSConfig, GetBucketReplicationMetrics, GetBucketReplicationMetricsV2, GetBucketReplicationResyncStatus, ResetBucketReplication, ResetBucketReplicationOnTarget, CancelBucketReplicationResync, CheckBucketReplication, HealthCheck, IsOnline, IsOffline, GetCreds, CredContext, UploadLimits, AlignedBuffer, FreeAlignedBuffer, IsRDMAAvailable; its tracing (TraceOn, TraceOff, TraceErrorsOnlyOn, TraceErrorsOnlyOff), SetAppInfo and NewCore, a second way to the same calls
  python  boto3's resource layer (`boto3.resource('s3')`, Bucket, Object, ObjectSummary and their collections), a second way to the same operations; the event system and `meta.events`; `close`, `can_paginate`, `waiter_names`, `get_waiter`: a waiter is a loop of `object_exists` or `bucket_exists` the program writes, with no closure to hand
  rust    the fluent builders and their `customize`, `send` and `presigned` (one function per operation here), and the SDK's config builder's other knobs (sleep, time source, interceptors, stalled stream protection, behavior version); rust-s3 set_dangerous_config and set_dangereous_config, which turn the certificate's check off, refused as `http` refuses it
